#
# One connection to the host-package helper, started by olivares-helper-apt.socket with the
# connection as standard input and output. The helper takes no argument and no path. It works only
# on the plan retained in its StateDirectory, root's and private: status verifies the retained RPMs
# with rpmkeys and rpm and reads the installed version; an act replays one retained native
# transaction (rpm -U of the signature-verified file), and is refused before it runs until the seam's guest proof
# is accepted. It fetches no package and has no network.
#
# The act's confinement is what rpm needs, measured on AlmaLinux 10 (rpm 4.19.1.1) under this unit with
# packages that have scriptlets, an account created by %pre, files owned by that account, a setgid file and
# a file with capabilities. The status read runs in the same template, so it holds them too.
# - The filesystem is writable (no ProtectSystem): a package installs under /usr, /etc, /var, /opt and
#   /boot. ProtectSystem=strict made rpm see read-only filesystems with no free space and refuse the transaction.
#   /home, /root, /tmp and /dev stay private or unreachable, and so do the kernel's interfaces.
# - RestrictSUIDSGID is not set: a package may install a set-id file, and with it set rpm fails with "chmod failed".
# - Five capabilities are rpm's own file operations and two are a scriptlet's change of account (the list is
#   in the unit tests, with the failure each one's absence causes). No other is held: no network, no module,
#   no mount, no CAP_SYS_ADMIN, no CAP_SYS_CHROOT. NoNewPrivileges keeps a child of rpm from gaining more, and
#   because exec can then gain nothing, the same capabilities are ambient: without that a scriptlet's setuid() fails.
# - MemoryDenyWriteExecute, PrivateDevices, PrivateNetwork and the rest are unchanged. Not measured: a package whose scriptlet
#   needs a device, a network, a JIT or a capability above is refused as a failed transaction (P1 failed or
#   partial), never half-hidden. The host-package path installs one non-kernel package, so those are the limits.
[Unit]
Description=Appliance host-package helper (one connection)
Documentation=https://github.com/olivaresai/olivares

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/libexec/olivares/olivares-portal-apt
User=root
StandardInput=socket
StandardOutput=socket
StandardError=journal
StateDirectory=olivares-package-plan
StateDirectoryMode=0700
RuntimeMaxSec=330
NoNewPrivileges=yes
ProtectSystem=no
ProtectHome=yes
PrivateTmp=yes
PrivateDevices=yes
PrivateNetwork=yes
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX
IPAddressDeny=any
ProtectClock=yes
ProtectHostname=yes
ProtectKernelTunables=yes
ProtectKernelModules=yes
ProtectKernelLogs=yes
ProtectControlGroups=yes
RestrictNamespaces=yes
RestrictRealtime=yes
LockPersonality=yes
MemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes
SystemCallArchitectures=native
CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_CHOWN CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE CAP_FOWNER CAP_FSETID CAP_SETFCAP CAP_SETGID CAP_SETUID
AmbientCapabilities=CAP_CHOWN CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE CAP_FOWNER CAP_FSETID CAP_SETFCAP CAP_SETGID CAP_SETUID
UMask=0077
